<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African mohair prices higher at 2nd summer sale.</title>
<headline>S.African mohair prices higher at 2nd summer sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH, South Africa 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mohair prices for the second summer sale were higher, the Mohair Board said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Of the 1,719 bales offered 47 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 2,400-3,302	(1,303-2,580)</p>
<p>		  medium     2,200-2,370	(2,210-2,210)</p>
<p>		  short	2,130-3,130	(2,052-2,600)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2,450-4,200	(2,700-5,000)</p>
<p>		  medium	   -		(    -    )</p>
<p>		  short	    -		(    -    )</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 6,000-11,000     (5,000-10,000)</p>
<p>		  medium     4,540-9,102	(4,300-3,700)</p>
<p>		  short	3,802-5,100	(2,700-4,800)</p>
<p>The third sale of the season is scheduled for April 8, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
